Subject: [PATCH 0011] GaussSeidel: accumulate corrections without copying source

F3 rounding change (not bit-identical). Write s for source[celli], i_j for
interface contributions in their existing update order, and l_j*psi_j for
lower-neighbour contributions in the existing forward-sweep scatter order.
Before diagonal division, with upper-neighbour terms still subtracted last:

  old: (((((s - i1) - i2) ...) - l1*psi1) - l2*psi2 ...) - u1*psi...;
  new: (s + (((((0 - i1) - i2) ...) - l1*psi1) - l2*psi2 ...))
       - u1*psi...;

Same terms and sweep order; the interface/lower sum is reassociated away from
s. The division and upper-neighbour loop are unchanged. Each cell resets its
accumulator before scattering only to larger indices, leaving zero between
sweeps/calls. Object calls retain a private zero-initialised field; the public
static entry point and batched component solver initialise their own fields
once per call. Shared matrix.work() is not used: symGaussSeidel also uses it
and leaves non-zero contents.

A multiply/subtract such as acc[u] -= lower*psii or psii -= upper*psi[u]
can contract to FMA if enabled. With -ffp-contract=off it cannot. Contrary to
the task's premise, this GCC 13.3 defaults to -ffp-contract=fast even with
-std=c++17; native FMA additionally requires suitable target flags. No compiler
flags are changed here. F3 Cd validation remains necessary.

